  "name": "start: do not exit non-zero after a session has already committed",
  "slug": "start-do-not-exit-non-zero-after-a-session-has-already-commi",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "After the withLock mutation commits (session created, ticket in_progress) and prints started ..., start calls buildContextPackData which uses the fail-fast listTickets/listSessions that reject on the FIRST corrupt file anywhere in the db. One unrelated bad file makes start exit non-zero even though it succeeded; an agent retries and hits activeSessionConflict (exit 6) on the very session it just started.",
    "details_md": "",
    "acceptance": [
      "The post-commit context-pack print reads via the tolerant path (listTicketsTolerant) or is wrapped so a render/read failure warns and still exits 0",
      "A test corrupts an unrelated ticket file, runs start on a good ticket, and asserts exit 0 with the session created"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/cli/commands/start.ts:272 buildContextPackData after lock release",
      "src/sessions/context-pack.ts:21,40 listTickets/listSessions (fail-fast)"
    ],
